# What the Rust generator writes that this repository does not want.
#
# See the Python ignore file for the reasoning; the same two kinds of line appear
# here.
#
# The hand-written helper — src/applab_ext.rs — is listed so regeneration never
# touches it. The generator does not produce it, but listing it is what keeps it
# safe if a future generator version decides to, and it records that the file is
# ours rather than the tool's.
#
# Cargo.toml and the generated runtime (src/apis/, src/models/) are NOT listed:
# Cargo.toml is what makes the crate build, and the generator rewrites it when the
# API changes. Its dependency list is maintained by the `cargo add` commands in
# the header comment of src/applab_ext.rs, not by this file — this file cannot
# protect it.

# Ours, protected from regeneration.
src/applab_ext.rs

# CI and publishing for a standalone project; this SDK lives inside AppLab.
.github/
git_push.sh
.travis.yml
.gitlab-ci.yml

# Documentation the generator emits alongside the code.
docs/

# The repository's own ignore rules are managed at the root.
# The generator's copy would be a second set that silently disagrees.
.gitignore
